<% content_for :title, "Sign up" %>

<%# Aligned with devise/sessions/new, which it did not resemble: no logo, no page title, a
    min-h-screen wrapper inside a <main> that already sits below a 64px header, and its own field
    and link spacing.

    Two real bugs went with it:

    - "Enter your email below to create an account" - the form asks for a *username*. This app
      authenticates on username (config.authentication_keys = [:username]) and a student may have
      no email at all.
    - `dark:text-slate-400` was the only dark: variant in the app, and .dark is defined in
      shadcn.css but nothing ever applies it. Tailwind v4 compiles dark: to
      @media (prefers-color-scheme: dark), so on any device with a dark OS setting that line
      rendered slate-400 over a background that stays light: **2.45:1**, a straight AA failure.
      The faint-text audit had recorded it as justified at "6.99:1 on dark" - a contrast against a
      dark background that never renders. %>
<div class="flex min-h-full flex-col justify-center py-12">
  <div class="mx-auto w-full max-w-sm">
    <div class="flex w-full justify-center">
      <%= image_tag "SITF-caponly-Logo.svg", class: "h-8 w-auto", alt: "Stocks in the Future" %>
    </div>

    <h1 class="pb-2 text-center text-2xl/9 font-bold tracking-tight text-slate-900">Create your account</h1>
    <p class="pb-4 text-center text-sm text-slate-600">
      Choose a username and password. You sign in with your username.
    </p>

      <%# `Ui::FormBuilder`, like every other form in the app. These four auth pages were the last on a
          third builder - `Shadcn::FormBuilder`, reached through `render_form_for` - which prepends its own
          base to whatever `class:` it is handed, so a field given `tw-input-primary` carried both strings
          and the shadcn one won on utility order. Sign in and sign up kept a 40px `rounded-md` field while
          every other form moved to 44px `rounded-lg`, and the markup read as though it were fixed.

          `w-full` on the submit stays: an auth card is one column and its action fills it, which is what
          Stripe, GitHub and Google all do on a sign-in page. %>
    <% opts = { as: resource_name, url: registration_path(resource_name), builder: Ui::FormBuilder } %>
    <%= form_for(resource, **opts) do |f| %>
      <div>
        <%= f.text_field :username,
                         label: "Username",
                         autofocus: true,
                         autocomplete: "username",
                         required: true %>

        <%= f.password_field :password,
                             label: "Password",
                             autocomplete: "new-password",
                             required: true %>

        <%= f.password_field :password_confirmation,
                             label: "Confirm password",
                             autocomplete: "new-password",
                             required: true %>

        <%# These were the shadcn render_button, whose --primary is a near-black navy, so the only
            off-brand primary button in the app was the one on the sign-up page. %>
        <%= f.submit "Sign up", class: "w-full" %>

        <div class="text-center">
          <%= link_to "Already have an account? Sign in", new_session_path(resource_name),
                      class: "tw-link-tap" %>
        </div>
      </div>
    <% end %>
  </div>
</div>
